  "scope": "Actual isolated initial and committed SIP private primary with independently admitted native consultant/held native remote, retained SIP with native private pair, and outside SIP/private physical-sibling exclusions. Six production methods each cover both EdDSA and ES256;48 actual SDK-verified frames validate. No whole-clause/task or other-role/profile qualification.",
  "implementation": [
    "Service selection preserves actual SIP/native origins and checks each selected endpoint\u2019s real audio-only Session. Same-intent private Core controls consume exact typed directional grants; SIP has no native signing surrogate.",
    "Fresh initial and committed SIP/native media and signal pairs share a physical-context seal, while named receive/send permissions remain separate. Registered candidate/primary/original-root/runtime and reciprocal private floors are required. Held remotes and same-Participant public physical siblings cannot inherit private authority.",
    "Only the original returning SIP primary may restore its captured public programme through the sealed return handle. Its consultant gets no return edge; other private pairs keep their own reciprocal physical floors, registered context and current permissions.",
    "Current outside-SIP capture excludes both active private physical slots before recipient freeze. The remaining public sibling keeps only its own Connection authority; no legacy fallback or new wire/HTTP route/schema is added."
  ],
